[[:db/retract 17592186347065 :question/answer-fields 17592186347066] {:db/id "q-161729/nonempty-fibers-v1/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "af8fc409-93f1-5b75-8606-5962e97972e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [17592186347067 17592186347068 17592186347069 17592186347070 17592186347071] :answer-field/correct 17592186347068 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186347065 :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,2\\le y\\le 2xz}.\n$$\n\nFor a fixed admissible $x$, let $[a(x),b(x)]$ be the full nonempty $z$ fiber of the exactly specified region $S$. Use ordered inner bounds and the actual outer $x$ range. What is $a(x)\\times b(x)$?" :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ is retained exactly. A nonempty $y$ fiber requires $2\\le2xz$, so $xz\\ge1$. The inequality $0\\le z\\le2x$ then forces $x>0$. For a fixed admissible $x$, combine these requirements to obtain\n\n$$\\frac1x\\le z\\le2x.$$\n\nThis interval is nonempty precisely when $1/x\\le2x$, giving $1/\\sqrt2\\le x\\le2$. Every point in this base admits $2\\le y\\le2xz$. Thus the full nonempty $z$ fiber has endpoints $a(x)=1/x$ and $b(x)=2x$, with\n\n$$a(x)b(x)=\\frac1x(2x)=2.$$\n\nThe valid repeated integral is\n\n$$\\iiint_S f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\int_{1/\\sqrt2}^{2}\\int_{1/x}^{2x}\\int_2^{2xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.$$\n\nFor $f=1$, integrating in $y$ and $z$ gives $4x^3-4x+1/x$, hence the volume is\n\n$$[x^4-2x^2+\\ln x]_{1/\\sqrt2}^{2}=\\frac{35}{4}+\\frac32\\ln2>0.$$\n\nThe authentic source solution copied the nominal pair $0,2x$ and reported its product $0$. Its formal repeated integral over $x\\in[-2,2]$ includes reversed and empty fibers; for $f=1$ it gives $0$, not the volume of $S$. The full nonempty fiber has endpoint product $2$." :db/ensure [:question/validate] :question/answer-fields ["q-161729/nonempty-fibers-v1/selection"]}]
